# n8n Twitch Node Project Structure

This is an n8n community node package for Twitch integration. The project follows n8n's standard node package structure.

## Core Files
- [index.js](mdc:index.js) - Main entry point (empty, used for package registration)
- [package.json](mdc:package.json) - Package configuration with n8n node definitions
- [tsconfig.json](mdc:tsconfig.json) - TypeScript configuration for strict compilation

## Directory Structure
- `nodes/Twitch/` - Contains all node implementations
  - [Twitch.node.ts](mdc:nodes/Twitch/Twitch.node.ts) - Main action node for Twitch API operations
  - [TwitchTrigger.node.ts](mdc:nodes/Twitch/TwitchTrigger.node.ts) - Webhook trigger node for Twitch events
  - [GenericFunctions.ts](mdc:nodes/Twitch/GenericFunctions.ts) - Shared API request functions
  - [twitch.svg](mdc:nodes/Twitch/twitch.svg) - Node icon
- `credentials/` - Contains credential definitions
  - [TwitchApi.credentials.ts](mdc:credentials/TwitchApi.credentials.ts) - Twitch API credentials configuration
- `dist/` - Compiled output directory (generated by build process)
- `docs/` - Documentation and screenshots

## Build Process
- TypeScript compilation: `npm run build` (compiles to `dist/`)
- Icon copying: Gulp task copies SVG/PNG files to dist
- Development: `npm run dev` for watch mode

## Package Configuration
The package exports two nodes:
1. `TwitchTrigger` - For webhook-based triggers (stream online/offline, follows, etc.)
2. `Twitch` - For API actions (search channels, get stream info, etc.)

Both nodes require `twitchApi` credentials for authentication.